w` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/components/ui/SparxNewTab.tsx:125:24\n  123 |       by: 'dev_trends',\n  124 |       score: 620,\n> 125 |       time: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) - 14400,\n      |                        ^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  126 |       url: 'https://news.ycombinator.com'\n  127 |     }\n  128 |   ]",["269","270"],["271","272"],"react-hooks/exhaustive-deps","React Hook useEffect has missing dependencies: 'initialFakeNews' and 'initialFakeRepos'. Either include them or remove the dependency array.","ArrayExpression",["273"],["274","275"],["276","277"],["278","279"],"Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Math.random` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/components/ui/scroll-morph-hero.tsx:270:11\n  268 |   const scatterPositions = useMemo(() => {\n  269 |     return IMAGES.map(() => ({\n> 270 |       x: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 1500,\n      |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  271 |       y: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 1000,\n  272 |       rotation: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 180,\n  273 |       scale: 0.6,","Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Math.random` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/components/ui/scroll-morph-hero.tsx:271:11\n  269 |     return IMAGES.map(() => ({\n  270 |       x: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 1500,\n> 271 |       y: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 1000,\n      |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  272 |       rotation: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 180,\n  273 |       scale: 0.6,\n  274 |       opacity: 0","Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Math.random` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/components/ui/scroll-morph-hero.tsx:272:18\n  270 |       x: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 1500,\n  271 |       y: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 1000,\n> 272 |       rotation: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 180,\n      |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  273 |       scale: 0.6,\n  274 |       opacity: 0\n  275 |     }))","react-hooks/set-state-in-effect","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/hooks/useAuth.ts:25:7\n  23 |     } catch (err) {\n  24 |       console.error('Firebase Auth Error', err)\n> 25 |       setIsAuthLoading(false)\n     |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  26 |       return () => {}\n  27 |     }\n  28 |   }, [])",["280","281"],"'error' is defined but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/hooks/useBrowser.ts:86:7\n  84 |     const active = tabs.find((t) => t.id === activeTabId)\n  85 |     if (active && !isUrlFocused) {\n> 86 |       setInputUrl(active.url === 'sparx://newtab' ? '' : active.url)\n     |       ^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  87 |     }\n  88 |   }, [activeTabId, tabs, isUrlFocused])\n  89 |",["282","283"],["284","285"],["286","287"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/hooks/useCloudSync.ts:26:26\n  24 |     // If user is not logged in, or PRIVACY MODE is active, abort the pull!\n  25 |     if (!user || isPrivacyMode) {\n> 26 |       if (isPrivacyMode) setCloudStatus('paused')\n     |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  27 |       return\n  28 |     }\n  29 |","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/app/sparx-ui/src/renderer/src/hooks/useCloudSync.ts:55:26\n  53 |     // If PRIVACY MODE is active, completely block data from leaving the app\n  54 |     if (!user || !hasLoadedFromCloud || isPrivacyMode) {\n> 55 |       if (isPrivacyMode) setCloudStatus('paused')\n     |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  56 |       return\n  57 |     }\n  58 |",{"messageId":"288","fix":"289","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"292","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"294","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"295","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"296","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"297","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"298","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"299","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"300","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"301","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"302","data":"303","fix":"304","desc":"305"},{"messageId":"302","data":"306","fix":"307","desc":"308"},{"messageId":"302","data":"309","fix":"310","desc":"311"},{"messageId":"302","data":"312","fix":"313","desc":"314"},{"messageId":"302","data":"315","fix":"316","desc":"305"},{"messageId":"302","data":"317","fix":"318","desc":"308"},{"messageId":"302","data":"319","fix":"320","desc":"311"},{"messageId":"302","data":"321","fix":"322","desc":"314"},{"messageId":"302","data":"323","fix":"324","desc":"305"},{"messageId":"302","data":"325","fix":"326","desc":"308"},{"messageId":"302","data":"327","fix":"328","desc":"311"},{"messageId":"302","data":"329","fix":"330","desc":"314"},{"messageId":"302","data":"331","fix":"332","desc":"305"},{"messageId":"302","data":"333","fix":"334","desc":"308"},{"messageId":"302","data":"335","fix":"336","desc":"311"},{"messageId":"302","data":"337","fix":"338","desc":"314"},{"messageId":"302","data":"339","fix":"340","desc":"341"},{"messageId":"302","data":"342","fix":"343","desc":"344"},{"messageId":"302","data":"345","fix":"346","desc":"347"},{"messageId":"302","data":"348","fix":"349","desc":"350"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"351","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"352","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"353","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"354","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"355","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"356","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"357","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"358","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"359","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"360","desc":"293"},{"desc":"361","fix":"362"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"363","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"364","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"365","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"366","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"367","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"368","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"369","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"370","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"371","desc":"290"},{"messageId":"291","fix":"372","desc":"293"},{"messageId":"288","fix":"373","